        <head>INSTRUCTIVE ENTERTIIINNEI</head>
        <p>INSTRUCTIVE ENTERTIIINNEI</p>
        <p>The Trades Exhibition opened at Parr 11 Warrington, this week, and whether fronl point of view of education, usefulness, or f; enjoyment, it provides exceptional opportun, to all classes in matters concerning our ell day requirements. Healthy entertainmeni blentled with interesting and instructive den strations, and at a cost of not exceeding penny the public are invited to attend accept the hospitality of the Syndicate. exhibition is not a profit-making concern, is held with the primary object of dernonst ing the value of well-known food preparati and the methods of preparing them for no' addition, there are displays of general 10,' hold requirements, and without any 01,10 the public are invited to inspect and Then there are forms of entertainment, ? orchestral music night and day, and the elOa tion generally is one of varied attractions of great value to all who are prepared to gl an opportunity. The main body of the e%b tion is provided by 17 members, many 6 whose names have become household throughout the English-speaking world.</p>
        <p>Messrs. Alfred Bird and Sons, Ltd., are re sented with a tastefully arranged stand,,, playing the world-famous Bird's Custard. Mange, and Crystal Jollies, made from the paration of the firm. Tasting samples are , plied and booklets distributed, containing 01 hundred recipes for the guidance of housed Separately, Messrs. Bird's have a very att tive stand displaying their recent product viz., Bird's S!pongie, a sponge mixture for 13 ing Swiss roll, Victoria sandwich, B,:c. At stand may be seen the Swiss roll being pared with the " Spongie," and tasting Barl of the actual result may be obtained. The in charge is always most happy to answer inquiries.</p>
        <p>Messrs. Bryant and May, Ltd., are a sense at least not " Matchless," for they dij a wonderful variety of matches, taper luminous boxes, the Swan vestas, Bird's Ell vestas, Ruby matches, and the 'special P safeties being prominent. All the latest improvements in incande gas..burners and mantles are displayed g exhibit of George Bray and Co., Ltd., of L A call at the "Bray" stand will afford the ir an opportunity of watching the demonstrg that are made hi proof of the fact thg,t economy is effected by adopting "Bray descent gas burners and mantles. At Cadbury Bros., Ltd., attractive 8 sample cups of their famous " Bourne/ Cocoa are-dispensed at the nominal char' one penny', and for this sum is included a d sample tin for home trial, also a sample uf equally famous and delicious " Bourql chodolate. .</p>
        <p>Cerelios, Ltd., show their well-known Salt, which never cakes, but always runs out of the dainty Cerebos pourer, so that IL be used to the Last grain. They also shot(i easy and quick it is to make delicious 6 agll for 3d.. cartons vallle and contaimrig samples of 'list° and their other preparstl" t</p>
        <p>witk4,fititg,, and E,:g iCd- contaimng</p>
        <p>Chivers and Sons Ltd., who by the waP been honoured lv being appointed purver jams and canned English .fruits to His 0 King George V., display their home-growl "ducts In a very attractive manner.'</p>
        <p>William Edge and Sons, Ltd. show /10 and econdmical it is to renew: Ltd., artie home dyeing. They give practical demo • tions with the famous Drummer Dyes, ordinary kitchen utensils. - As Warrington. is the place of early rise bard workers, the assistants at .The " r Stand are showing how to. serve a meal, moment with the toasted wheat fial "Force" and hot milk. No cooking , quired with this food. All Warrington • wives Ahould pay a visit to this stand. The Hovis-Bread Flour Co., Ltd., disl fine collection of edibles baked frote Flour, including Hovis Bread, which ch like 'in preference to cake. John Mackintosh, Ltd., show a good Coll 'rom their Halifax Toffee Mills, pr 0,0,,</p>
        <p>_ features being the new Toffee de Luxe, Milk Toffee.</p>
