      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0052" n="art0052">
        <head>BIRTHS. MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</head>
        <p>BIRTHS. MARRIAGES. DEATHS.</p>
        <p>Notices of births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in the " Examiner" at the following rates :—Not exceeding 20 words, is. 6d. each; every additional seven words, 6d.</p>
        <p>Deaths. MERCHANT.—April 6th, at 23, Wellfield-street, James Albert Merchant, aged 24 years. CLAHE.—ApriI 6th, at 21, Norman-street, Martha Crare, aged 75 years. YOUNG.—April 7th, at 84, Pierpoint-street, John Yortng. aged 66 years. In Memoriam. • snE,AnEn.—ln loving memory of Mary Ellen, wife of Basil Shearer, who died April 9th, 1913. HUSBAND and FAMILY. 26, Crosfield-street, Warrington.</p>
