      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0101" n="art0101">
        <head>LAND.</head>
        <p>THE LAND.</p>
        <p>t</p>
        <p>SECOND ARTICLE.</p>
        <p>OUR PRESENT RATING SYSTEM.</p>
        <p>caricaturing. .a z —MR. LLOYD GEORGE at MIDI),</p>
        <p>THE JUDGE (to the producer) : • "After reviewing the evidence brought before me it is evident that you, Sir, have been guilty of expending labour -and capital on your land .it is therefore my duty to fine (rate) you ten pounds, and I must warn you that the penalty will be re-imposed next year if you persist in your efforts. Had you, like the gentleman on my right, allowed your land to be used as the last resting place for defunct felines and discarded receptacles, you would have escaped this penalty."</p>
