      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0182" n="art0182">
        <head>BOWLING.</head>
        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>WORKS ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>" Finlayson" Cup Competition Draw.</p>
        <p>We are glad to note that the Warrington Works Amateur Bowling Association has be- come so popular that this year there is a record entry of 72 teams. The next best to this was in 1912, when 63 teams entered. The Association are in the happy position of having the largest number of teams entering a competition of this kind in Great Britain. The draw for the first round of the competition was made at the Horse and :Jockey HOtel on Tuesday evening, and •is appended. Secretaries are requested to have teams up to the times stated, and thus assist the Council. The Merit Competition (individual) will be played again during the season, and fur- ther particulars will be given later. Owing to the lengthy season and to the, fact that the green has been partly relaid during the winter, Mr. Rushworth has decided not to open the green until April 16th. The following is the draw for the preliminary round, to be played April 18th, commencing at 1.40 p.m.:—</p>
        <p>I.4o—Fir-GI Mattress No. 2 v. Walker's No. 2. 2.3o—Ryland? No.-4 V. Crosfield's Tin Dept. 3.2o—Crosfield's No. I.v. Crosfield's Glycerine. 4.10—L. and N.-W. Railway v. Cheshire Lines. s.o—Richmond's (Grappenliall) V. Whiteeross Wire Drawers. _ _</p>
        <p>..50--Grappenhall Tannery v. St. Helens Cable No. 2.</p>
        <p>Referee, J. Willett. Assistants, H. HaHord and J. Howarth.</p>
