        <p>3.4o—Bewsey Wire Ropery v. Alliance Box Co. 4.3o—Richmond's (Academy-street) v. Fennel- street Tannery. s.2o—Rylands No. 4 or Crosfield's Tin v. Pen- keth Tannery. 6.10—P. and K. Boiler Yard v. Randall Bros.' Tannery. Referee, T. Humphreys. Assistants, A. Peckitt and F. Dale.</p>
        <p>. May 2nd. 2.o—Rylands' Apprentices v. Guest* Bros.'. Tannery. 2.so—Warrington Printers v. Rylands' No. 2. 3.4o—Warrington Tannery v. Whitecross Engi- neers.</p>
        <p>4.3o—Crosfield's (Cheshire) v. Crosfield's No. 1 or Crosfield's Glycerine. ' s.2o—Ship Canal (Bridgewater Department) v. Howley Tannery. 6.lo—Stockton Heath Forge v. Assurance Agents. 7.0-st. Helens Cabld No. 1 v. Thewlis and Griffith? No. 1. Referee, F. Dean, Assistants, W. Robinson and</p>
