      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0184" n="art0184">
        <head>WARRINGTON ATHLETIC CLUB.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON ATHLETIC CLUB.</p>
        <p>A NEW JUNIOR SECTION. Warrington Athletic Club held a special general meeting at the Pavilion on Tuesday last, and it was decided to form a junior section, with a view to assisting those already identified with, or intending to participate in, such estimable movements as the League of the Cross, Boy Scouts, Church Lads' Brigade, Territorials, &amp;c., and particularly those desirous of competing for the 8.0. proficiency badges. The junior section is to be confined to youths over 16 and under 19 years, with an annual subscription of one shil- ling. A few years ago sports meetings were held an- nually by the Football Club, Police Athletic Club, and Warrington Charities Committee. Last season, excepting the military sports, only two meetings were held, one open and one mem- bers' meeting, both by Warrington Athletic Club, with a desire to cater for local.athletes, ; but unfortunate Weather conditions rendered the efforts unratisfactory from the financial point of view. This season nothing has been arranged yet; and it is to be hoped that the Athletic Club will make another effort; the occasion of their annual social and prize distribution, on the 25th inst., should provide a good opportunity for dis- cussing the matter, and as it may be remem- bered that a number of the Lancashire County Championships have yet to be allocated, the local public should be provided with another opportunity to patronise amateur sport.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-11_WidnesExaminer_art0185" n="art0185">
