        <p>GpA about llEflns and How to Use Them, free; send for one.—Trimnell, The Herbalist, 14i, Richmond-road, Cardiff. Estab- lished 1879.</p>
        <p>The theme of the comedy is that loving, over. strict Nonconformist parents forget that theft children have reached the age of Manhood and continue to treat them as irresponsible. The children revolt, and in the end gain their own way. Whether it is the right way or the wrong way, the audience must decide for themselves, for the parents cannot solve the problem; aftei all, their dogmatism they have learned to wonder "whether they have been right, aftei all."</p>
        <p>fasting is simply The acting, the staging, and even the break- There will be a matinee on Monday at 2.30. ply perfection. PRISON REFORMER'S PLAY.</p>
        <p>An adaptation from Charles Reade's novel, "It's Never Too Late To Mend," is the attrac- tion at the Royal Court Theatre this week, and although the play has been " potted " to be presented twice nightly, many salient points and gripping situations are retained. The strongest element is the exposure of the cruel prison system, but a story of love and adventure, although not of the orthodox kind, is also a pleasing feature. Mr. Andrew Emms' company distinguished themselves in the play.</p>
