        <p>PUBLIC AMUSEMENTS. "THE YOUNGER GENERATION" AT ROYAL COURT. ftepertoire companies all over the country have done something for the intellectual drama, but before the general public will be drawn to see their work they must learn that the succes: of a play depends as much upon humour that it contains as upon the gloomy outlook it portrays. "The Younger Generation" is a humorous play; it is a real and a great comedy, and its great success at the Haymarket Theatre, Lon- don, is being re-echoed throughout the pro- vinces. In "Hindle Wakes" Mr. Stanley Houghton opened a new era in plays, but his "Younger Generation" is a better play than this, and without any questionable sensational outcome.</p>
